 "literal": "Dewy bush climbed green-creeper field-bean / parrot beak resembling bright-emitting many flowers / wild-cat tooth form-of with-jasmine mingled / north-wind having-come-of on-top-of-that pain to-afflict / behold! may-you-live-long friend clear-waves / ocean deep like-a-ship appearing / evening disappears his sapphire tall hill indeed",
 "translation": "Look, my friend, may you live long! On top of the cold north wind coming to batter me with pain, his sapphire-like tall hill—which appears like a ship sinking in the deep ocean of clear waves—now disappears in the evening, just as the field-bean creepers that climbed the dewy bushes open their many bright flowers resembling parrots' beaks, mingled with jasmine buds shaped like wild cats' teeth.",
 "modern": "பனி படர்ந்த புதர்களில் படர்ந்துள்ள பசிய அவரைக்கொடியின் கிளிகளின் மூக்கைப் போன்ற ஒளிவீசும் பல மலர்களும், காட்டுப்பூனையின் பற்களைப் போன்ற முல்லை அரும்புகளும் கலந்து மலர்கின்றன. இந்த வேளையில், வாடைக்காற்று வந்து என் துயரத்தை மேலும் அதிகமாக்குகிறது. தோழியே! தெளிந்த அலைகளைக் கொண்ட கடலில் மூழ்கும் கப்பலைப் போலத் தோன்றி, மாலைப் பொழுதில் மெல்ல மறைகின்ற அவருடைய நீலமணி போன்ற உயர்ந்த மலையை நீ காண்பாயாக!",
 "explanation": "The heroine is speaking to her confidante during the evening of the Mullai season, when the hero was expected to return. She points out that the field-bean flowers, resembling parrot beaks, and jasmine buds, resembling wild cat teeth, are blooming together on the dewy bushes. On top of this seasonal change, the cold north wind has arrived to intensify her pain of separation. She looks at the hero's distant sapphire-like tall hill, which is gradually disappearing in the evening mist. The hill looks like a ship sinking into the deep ocean of clear waves, symbolizing her fading hope and sinking heart as night falls without him.",
